# 📊 Marketing Funnel & Conversion Analysis

## 📌 Project Overview

This project focuses on analyzing marketing campaign data to understand customer conversion behavior, identify areas where potential customers are lost, and support better business decisions.

## 🎯 Objectives

The main objectives of this analysis were to:

* Examine patterns in customer conversion
* Determine where customers drop off within the marketing funnel
* Assess the effectiveness of different campaigns
* Develop practical recommendations based on the findings

## 🛠 Tools Used

* Power BI
* Data analysis techniques
* Business intelligence

## 📊 Key Analysis Performed

* Conversion rate analysis
* Marketing funnel analysis (Total → Engaged → Converted)
* Campaign performance evaluation
* Conversion analysis by job role

## 📈 Key Insights

* Although a large number of customers were contacted, only a relatively small proportion ultimately converted.
* Customer engagement, particularly call duration, has an important influence on conversion.
* Conversion performance differs across various job categories.
* Making too many campaign contacts can negatively affect campaign effectiveness.

## 💡 Recommendations

* Prioritize customer segments that demonstrate higher conversion rates.
* Strengthen engagement approaches during the first customer interaction.
* Avoid unnecessary or excessive follow-up contacts.
* Improve campaign targeting to focus resources on customers with greater conversion potential.

## 📁 Project Files

* Power BI Dashboard (`.pbix`)
* Dataset (`.csv`)

